      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes a mechanism that records the prior state of files before they are overwritten by the guarded tool executor. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core purpose**: Before any file is written, the system journals (records) its previous state \u2014 either the file\u0027s original content if it existed, or a note that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n**Rollback capability**: If an agent run fails (due to turn cap exceeded, an unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can reverse all recorded writes in reverse order: restoring previous file content or deleting newly created files.\n\n**Transaction semantics**: This provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the in-memory journal itself acts as the transaction log for the duration of a single run.\n\n**Query agent note**: The Query agent (which is what\u0027s running this conversation) doesn\u0027t use the rollback path since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
